## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/interpolated-iv

Interpolated IV

Returns the Interpolated IV for a given trading day. If there is no expiration then the data is calcualted via linear interpolation
with the next 2 closest expirations

Date must be the current or a past date. If no date is given, returns data for the current/last market day.


### Fully resolved operation
```json
{
  "key": "GET /api/stock/{ticker}/interpolated-iv",
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/api/stock/{ticker}/interpolated-iv",
  "transport": "http-rest",
  "operation": {
    "callbacks": {},
    "description": "Returns the Interpolated IV for a given trading day. If there is no expiration then the data is calcualted via linear interpolation\nwith the next 2 closest expirations\n\nDate must be the current or a past date. If no date is given, returns data for the current/last market day.\n",
    "operationId": "PublicApi.TickerController.interpolated_iv",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "description": "",
        "in": "path",
        "name": "ticker",
        "required": true,
        "schema": {
          "description": "A single ticker",
          "example": "AAPL",
          "title": "SingleTicker",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      {
        "description": "",
        "in": "query",
        "name": "date",
        "required": false,
        "schema": {
          "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
          "example": "2024-01-18",
          "title": "Optional Market Date",
          "type": "string"
        }
